<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct copper imports surge 414.63 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct copper imports surge 414.63 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined copper imports in October surged to 130,557 tonnes, up 414.63 percent from 25,369 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Thursday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Oct 96	   Sept 96	 Oct 95</p>
<p> Total	   130,557	  29,794	  25,369</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Chile	     8,789	  10,129	  13,009</p>
<p> U.S.		5,169	   4,371	   3,551</p>
<p> Zambia	  105,222	   7,083	   3,172</p>
<p>Imports in the first 10 months of 1996 were 402,024 tonnes, against 336,529 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 7391)</p>
</text>
